meta:
  title: Privacy
  description: "What Toronto Trees collects, which is essentially nothing."
  og_image: /og-default.png

options: null

content:
  heading: Privacy
  sections[4]{heading,body}:
    What we collect,"Nothing. Toronto Trees is a static website with no accounts, no forms, and no analytics. Nothing about your visit is stored or transmitted to us."
    Cookies,"None. The site sets no cookies and uses no local storage for tracking."
    Third parties,"Loading the map fetches basemap tiles from OpenFreeMap (backed by OpenStreetMap) and vector tile data from Cloudflare R2. Those providers see standard HTTP request information (IP address, user agent, referring page) as with any web request. Their own policies apply to those interactions."
    Contact,"Questions or feedback may be sent by creating an <a href=\"https://github.com/orvn/toronto-trees/issues/new\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">issue on GitHub</a>."
